# Research Agent — Project Context

Local-first Python 3.11+ CLI (`research`) for paper understanding with multi-agent Analyst + Critic.

## Package layout (`src/research_agent/`)

| Module | Epic | Responsibility |
|--------|------|----------------|
| `cli.py` | E1.1/E1.5 | Typer commands |
| `config.py` | E1.1 | `~/.research-agent/config.yaml` |
| `agents/` | E1.3+ | Orchestrator, Analyst, Critic, Searcher, Scribe, MemoryKeeper |
| `core/` | E1.2/E1.3 | LLM client, Paper, Idea entities |
| `parsers/` | E1.2 | PyMuPDF PDF parsing |
| `storage/` | E1.2/E1.4 | SQLite + ChromaDB |
| `search/` | E1.2/E3.1 | arXiv, Semantic Scholar, GitHub |
| `ui/` | E5.2 | Textual TUI |

## Constraints

- Data stays under `~/.research-agent/` (config, SQLite, Chroma, PDF cache).
- Default LLM: DeepSeek via OpenAI-compatible SDK; abstract behind `LLMProvider` when adding providers.
- Critic: never score 10; score &lt; 7 must include reasons.
- Implement only the current epic scope; stub files are placeholders — do not flesh out future epics early.

## Planning source of truth

`planning/architecture.md`, `planning/milestones/m1-paper-understanding.md`.
